msgid "verification.mail.subject"
msgstr "Confirm the e-mail address of an OpenFESL account"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "verification.mail.body"
msgstr ""
"An OpenFESL account was registered with this e-mail address. It can sign in and log in from games once the address is confirmed. This link opens a page whose button confirms it:\n"
"\n"
"{link}\n"
"\n"
"The link is valid until {expires}. After that, signing in on the site offers a new link, and the next login from a game sends one.\n"

msgid "account.mail.proof.subject"
msgstr "Link a sign-in service to an OpenFESL account"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "account.mail.proof.body"
msgstr ""
"A sign-in through {service} asked to link it to the OpenFESL account {account}. This link opens a page whose button links {service} and signs in:\n"
"\n"
"{link}\n"
"\n"
"The link is valid until {expires} and works once. Without it, nothing changes.\n"

msgid "account.mail.address.subject"
msgstr "Confirm the e-mail address of an OpenFESL account"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "account.mail.address.body"
msgstr ""
"An OpenFESL account was registered with this e-mail address and can already sign in. This link opens a page whose button confirms the address:\n"
"\n"
"{link}\n"
"\n"
"The link is valid until {expires}.\n"

msgid "account.mail.in_use.subject"
msgstr "Registration with the address of an OpenFESL account"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "account.mail.in_use.body"
msgstr ""
"A registration with this e-mail address was sent on {sent}, but the address already has an OpenFESL account. Nothing was changed and no service was linked. The account signs in at:\n"
"\n"
"{link}\n"
"\n"
"Its account page links services. A forgotten game password is reset at:\n"
"\n"
"{reset}\n"

msgid "account.mail.reset.subject"
msgstr "Set a new game password for an OpenFESL account"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "account.mail.reset.body"
msgstr ""
"A new game password was requested for the OpenFESL account with this e-mail address. This link sets it:\n"
"\n"
"{link}\n"
"\n"
"It is valid until {expires} and works once. Without it, the game password stays as it is.\n"

msgid "account.mail.deletion.subject"
msgstr "OpenFESL account deactivated"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "account.mail.deletion.body"
msgstr ""
"The OpenFESL account {name} with this e-mail address was deactivated on {at}, as a deletion request on the site asked. It no longer signs in on the site or logs in to games. An admin completes the deletion of the account with everything on it; until then, only an admin can withdraw the request.\n"

